# =============================================================================
# ~/.claude — what may be committed
#
# DESIGN: block everything, then allow named files only.
# Written this way on purpose. If a new file appears in this folder later —
# a cache, a log, a credential — it is excluded automatically instead of
# relying on someone remembering to exclude it.
#
# NEVER let these in (all blocked by the rule below; listed so the reason is on record):
#   .claude.json         account UUIDs, machine ID, every folder ever opened
#   history.jsonl        every prompt typed, plus pasted content
#   projects/**/*.jsonl  ~158 MB of full session transcripts
#   .credentials.json    login token (not present today — creds are in the macOS Keychain)
#   backups/             copies of .claude.json
#   plugins/ skills/     account-keyed; regenerate on login. Committing them
#                        would carry one account's UUID into another.
#   file-history/ paste-cache/   snapshots of your files and clipboard
# =============================================================================

# Block everything
*

# --- allow: the ignore file itself, and the rebuild instructions
!.gitignore
!README.md

# --- allow: global rules (the point of this repo)
!CLAUDE.md
!STANDARDS.md
!RTK.md
!REPOS.md
!PROJECTS.md
!OLLAMA.md
!ENVIRONMENT.md
!SETUP-PLAN.md
!PHASE2-REMOVALS.md
!PHASE2C-REMOVALS.md
!PHASE2C-REMOVALS.json

# --- allow: settings and statusline
!settings.json
!statusline/
!statusline/context.py

# --- allow: copies of what each project keeps out of its own repo (6.3 / D13) —
#     its CLAUDE.md and its permission rules — so they travel without going into
#     each project's own git. Named files only: a project folder here must never
#     pull in anything except the files listed below. Skills are deliberately
#     absent; they were judged to travel in the projects' own repos. Not verified
#     per project — see project-rules/README.md.
!project-rules/
!project-rules/*/
!project-rules/*/CLAUDE.md
!project-rules/*/.claude/
!project-rules/*/.claude/settings.json
!project-rules/*/.claude/settings.local.json
!project-rules/README.md
!project-rules/manifest.tsv
!project-rules/sync.sh
!project-rules/drift.sh

# --- allow: archive/ — things that cannot be recreated, so they must survive this
#     machine. backups/ stays ignored and local; anything that has to outlive the
#     Mac goes here instead. Named files only, same rule as project-rules/.
!archive/
!archive/README.md
!archive/*.bundle
!archive/*.tar.gz

# --- allow: baselines/ — dated behaviour baselines, compared run to run. Two
#     lines because git will not descend into an excluded directory, so the
#     folder and the file pattern each need an exception.
!baselines/
!baselines/*.md

# --- allow: memory files ONLY. Session transcripts sit in the same tree
#     and must stay out, so this walks in by directory and takes .md only.
!projects/
!projects/*/
!projects/*/memory/
!projects/*/memory/*.md

# --- allow: hand-written global skills, by name.
#     `skills/` is blocked above because `skills/synced/` is account-keyed and
#     regenerates on login. A skill written by hand here is neither — it carries
#     no account UUID, and it would simply be lost on an account switch, which is
#     the thing this repo exists to prevent. Named files only, so `synced/` and
#     anything else that appears under `skills/` stay out automatically.
!skills/
!skills/ollama/
!skills/ollama/SKILL.md

# --- allow: templates read on demand (STANDARDS.md § How a task runs).
#     Named files only, same rule as project-rules/.
!templates/
!templates/new-project.md
!templates/roadmap.md
!templates/deferred-improvements.md
!templates/handoff.md

# --- allow: harness/ — the setup's control desk (D33). Named files only.
!harness/
!harness/status.md
!harness/cross-check.md
!harness/session-check.sh

# --- allow: the setup-only rules file (D33). .claude/ also holds current-task.md
#     and settings.local.json, which stay ignored — `*` still matches them.
!.claude/
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
